{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":292,"output":642,"cacheRead":14656,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18,"totalTokens":15590,"cost":{"input":0.00028207199999999997,"output":0.0019491120000000002,"cacheRead":0.0028315392,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005062723200000001}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done. Only the three permitted files changed; all 10 tests pass.\n\n## Root cause\n`event-projector.mjs` used a single global `pending` promise chain with two compounding defects:\n1. **State committed before persistence** — `states.set(...)` ran *before* `await applyToStore(...)`, so a transient store rejection still mutated state, and the rejection propagated into the shared `pending` promise. The next `pending.then(...)` skipped its callback and re-rejected, poisoning later events for that trade.\n2. **One global queue** — every `project()` call (across all trades) appended to the same chain, so a slow store call for one trade blocked unrelated, ready trades.\n\n## Repair (`event-projector.mjs`)\n- Replaced the global chain with a **per-trade** `queues` map; same-trade events still serialize in call order, different trades progress concurrently.\n- Compute + validate the next state, then `await applyToStore(...)` **first**, and only `states.set(...)` on success — a rejection leaves state untouched.\n- Swallow rejections on the per-trade serialization chain (`run.then(noop, noop)`) so a failure can't poison later work; the caller still sees the rejection.\n- Added `applyEvent` validation: first event must be `CREATED` v1; later events must be `current.version + 1`; duplicate/stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting; version gaps reject; `CANCELLED` is terminal; `CREATED`/`AMENDED` require positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`; unsupported types reject with `TypeError`.\n- All snapshots, store arguments, returned states, and the event passed to `applyToStore` are `structuredClone` copies, so mutable internal state never leaks; protected fields can't be overwritten by an amend payload.\n\n## Tests added (`student-tests.mjs`)\nEight meaningful regression cases (plus the two committed ones = 10 total):\n1. Unrelated trades progress concurrently (gate-based; fails on the old global queue).\n2. Duplicate/stale version returns current snapshot without persisting.\n3. Version gap rejects without changing state.\n4. `CANCELLED` is terminal and rejects later new versions.\n5. `CREATED` with invalid notional rejects without persisting.\n6. `AMENDED` with invalid field rejects and leaves prior state intact.\n7. Unsupported event type rejects with `TypeError`.\n8. Snapshots and store arguments are isolated from internal state (mutations don't leak).\n\n## Visible test result\n```\nℹ tests 10   ℹ pass 10   ℹ fail 0   ℹ duration_ms ~64\n```\n\n## Remaining risk\n- No retry logic; callers must re-submit the same event after a transient store failure (safe, since state is unchanged).\n- `structuredClone` requires cloneable payloads (the synthetic fixture only produces plain JSON-like events).\n- Field validation is strict (no numeric-string coercion) to keep behavior predictable."}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All tests pass, only the three allowed files changed. Let me write the final summary.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Done. Only the three permitted files changed; all 10 tests pass.\n\n## Root cause\n`event-projector.mjs` used a single global `pending` promise chain with two compounding defects:\n1. **State committed before persistence** — `states.set(...)` ran *before* `await applyToStore(...)`, so a transient store rejection still mutated state, and the rejection propagated into the shared `pending` promise. The next `pending.then(...)` skipped its callback and re-rejected, poisoning later events for that trade.\n2. **One global queue** — every `project()` call (across all trades) appended to the same chain, so a slow store call for one trade blocked unrelated, ready trades.\n\n## Repair (`event-projector.mjs`)\n- Replaced the global chain with a **per-trade** `queues` map; same-trade events still serialize in call order, different trades progress concurrently.\n- Compute + validate the next state, then `await applyToStore(...)` **first**, and only `states.set(...)` on success — a rejection leaves state untouched.\n- Swallow rejections on the per-trade serialization chain (`run.then(noop, noop)`) so a failure can't poison later work; the caller still sees the rejection.\n- Added `applyEvent` validation: first event must be `CREATED` v1; later events must be `current.version + 1`; duplicate/stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting; version gaps reject; `CANCELLED` is terminal; `CREATED`/`AMENDED` require positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`; unsupported types reject with `TypeError`.\n- All snapshots, store arguments, returned states, and the event passed to `applyToStore` are `structuredClone` copies, so mutable internal state never leaks; protected fields can't be overwritten by an amend payload.\n\n## Tests adde